Gate local quorum on durability and application on explicit prerequisites

Pinned willemt/raft delta: optional durable_idx and before_apply hooks.
Null callbacks preserve historical behavior for those optional hooks.
CP-043 adds native RAFT_ERR_PERSIST_PENDING=-9, propagated before the applied
index advances, and propagates candidate self-vote callback errors before
RequestVote emission. Correct callback-error propagation deliberately changes
the failed-self-vote path; it does not claim V1 is byte-for-byte unchanged.
Optional log_prepare_truncate runs once before whole-suffix deletion; a pending
return leaves the existing pop loop untouched. Null hook preserves the old path.
Permanent regression: tests/v2_raft_persistence_tests.cpp.

CP-070 (M3 log finding 40): raft_send_appendentries_all no longer abandons the
remaining peers at the first failing one, and a peer behind the snapshot gets
an empty append at the snapshot point from the periodic heartbeat, so it stays
a quiet follower instead of campaigning and deposing a healthy leader.
Permanent regression: the stranded-voter test in tests/v2_replication_tests.cpp.

CP-073 (M3 log finding 41): raft_get_last_log_term falls back to the snapshot term
when the log is compacted to its end, as the voter side already does; before,
such a candidate advertised term 0 and no voter would ever elect it.
Permanent regression: the compacted-election test in tests/v2_replication_tests.cpp.

CP-076 (M3 log findings 43 and 47): optional pre-vote (Raft thesis 9.6), enabled
by raft_set_prevote and off by default. An expired election timer opens a
pre-vote round for current_term + 1 without touching term, vote or log; a voter
grants only if it has not heard from a leader within the election timeout and
the asker's log is at least as up-to-date, and granting changes nothing; only a
majority of grants for the proposed term starts the real election. A refusal
carrying a newer term brings the asker to that term. msg_requestvote_t and
msg_requestvote_response_t gain a trailing prevote flag, so every transport must
carry it before enabling. raft_private.h gains the two pre-vote fields.
Permanent regression: the pre-vote tests in tests/v2_replication_tests.cpp and
tests/v2_durable_quorum_tests.cpp.

The patch is generated against the RAFT_COMMIT base using zero-context diffs.
CMake verifies exact patched source hashes; do not edit generated build sources
as the only record of a fork change.

